-- A module whose one error is a value cycle reports that cycle and nothing
-- else (checker-v2.md §13.1 as amended by the review of R2a, S2). `r` is
-- defined in terms of itself through a record field, which is
-- `cyclic_value`; and v1 gives the `r` inside it an evidence argument (the
-- `==`'s `strict_eq`) that `r`, which has no requirements, does not take.
-- R2a's first I7 assert ran BEFORE `Cycles`, saw a module with
-- no error yet, and added an INTERNAL ERROR at that `r` to the cycle
-- message. The assert now runs last, gated on every error the module
-- reported, so the golden holds the cycle alone. On 9a931d7: the cycle
-- alone, as here.
r =
    { f = \x -> if x == 0 then 0 else r.f (x - 1) }
